# Role
You are the single integration point between TinyWins and the Band Agent
API (sponsor track) — the web side of the Goal Room loop. The Python
worker in `services/band-worker/` is the receiving side: it gets @mentions
from Band and relays them as HMAC-signed callbacks to
`/api/internal/band/*`. Nothing else in the app may call Band directly.

# Requirements
Write these exported functions in `src/lib/band.ts`, all sharing one
`bandRequest` helper that targets `https://app.band.ai/api/v1/agent`,
authenticates with the `X-API-Key` header (`BAND_COACH_API_KEY` by
default), throws a clear error naming the env var when the key is absent,
and surfaces non-OK responses as thrown errors including the HTTP status.
Responses unwrap Band's `{ data: T }` envelope.

1. `createBandGoalRoom(title)` — creates a Band chat titled
   `TinyWins · <title>`, adds the Reflection Guide agent
   (`BAND_REFLECTION_AGENT_ID`) as a participant, returns the room id.
2. `sendBandRoomMessage({ roomId, content, mentions })` — posts one
   message into a room.
3. `requestGoalReflection({ roomId, goalId, checkInId })` — the check-in
   hook. Content must be **pure JSON** `{"goalId","checkInId"}` (no prose):
   the worker `json.loads`es message content and relays it verbatim to
   `/api/internal/band/reflections`, which requires exactly those fields.
   Mentions: `[BAND_REFLECTION_AGENT_ID]`. Throws a named error if that
   env var is unset.

Failure semantics: callers treat every throw as non-blocking — a check-in
must never fail because Band is down (labeled log only, no hidden retry,
per the "no hidden fakes" rule).

# Dependencies
None — sibling of `llm.ts`/`tts.ts`; consumed by the goals check-in route.

# Acceptance criteria (see tests/band.test.ts)
- `createBandGoalRoom` POSTs `/chats` then `/chats/{id}/participants` with
  the reflection agent id, sending `X-API-Key`, and returns the room id.
- `sendBandRoomMessage` POSTs `/chats/{roomId}/messages` with content and
  mentions in Band's `{ message: ... }` envelope.
- `requestGoalReflection` sends parseable-JSON content containing exactly
  `goalId` and `checkInId`, mentioning the reflection agent.
- A missing `BAND_COACH_API_KEY` or `BAND_REFLECTION_AGENT_ID` throws an
  error naming that variable.
- A non-OK Band response throws an error containing the HTTP status.
